WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:04.480
Speaker 1: This is really one of the most
remarkable confrontations of a Republican

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:10.700
delusion that I've seen in a long time, and
it took place on Fox News, no doubt.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:18.369
A Fox News host, Neil Cavuto, asked former
Republican Senator Kelly Lefler remember her

00:00:18.369 --> 00:00:25.169
really the perfect question about her claims
that there were problems and irregularities

00:00:25.169 --> 00:00:32.380
in the 2020 election in Georgia in which she
was a candidate and lost to Raphael Warnock.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.630
And the question is really simple.

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:40.600
If there were problems with the Trump vs.
Biden results and they can't be trusted because

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:45.800
the Georgia secretary of state, Brad Raffensperger,
was a partizan and biased arbiter of that

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:50.250
election, he supported you, Kelly Lefler,
in that race.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.390
What does that mean?

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.290
Isn't that an obvious conflict?

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:58.430
Now, remember that I brought this up, a similar
version of this back in November, just after

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:04.190
the election when I tweeted, quote, Why have
Trump and Republicans accepted the results

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:07.990
from House and Senate elections, but not presidential?

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:10.190
Everything was on the same ballots.

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:15.110
In other words, tons of Republicans who won
in the House and Senate on the same ballots

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:18.630
as where Trump lost were saying, we cannot
trust these results.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:19.870
It's rigged.

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:22.180
This there's all sorts of irregularities.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.180
But so hold on.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.810
We also can't trust that you won.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:25.810
Right.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:30.240
And of course, that's not what they were talking
about, an obvious problem with their argument.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:37.350
So let's now get to the video of Neil Cavuto,
who reduces Carly Lefler to mumbling and stumbling

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:41.880
by pointing out, you know, the guy you're
saying needs to be investigated for his role

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.380
in the election.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.340
He supported you in that race.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:52.260
And, of course, part of the implication here
is maybe he did something screwy to help you

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:53.260
as well.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:54.260
Right.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:55.260
Take a look at this.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:58.050
Just a remarkable 60 seconds of footage making
sure that

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.700
Speaker 3: everyone's voice is heard.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:05.630
Speaker 4: All right, so if we have an investigation
into that, it would be investigations after

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:10.879
other investigations, this one more focused,
I guess, on the behavior of Mr. Raffensperger.

00:02:10.879 --> 00:02:17.010
But you would charge that you want to probe
into whether he used his office to advance

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:19.189
his political interests.

00:02:19.189 --> 00:02:23.549
He was supporting you and your colleague.

00:02:23.549 --> 00:02:29.030
So how was that opposite what your interests
were?

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:31.299
You were both on the same page.

00:02:31.299 --> 00:02:35.030
Speaker 3: That's not exactly correct.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:40.519
I mean, look, he's our top election official,
he's not a partizan official per say, but

00:02:40.519 --> 00:02:44.400
Speaker 4: he wasn't for this, but he wasn't
for your opponent, right, Senator?

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.400
He was for you.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.940
He was for Senator Purdue.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:50.269
And what would be in his interest to sabotage
that?

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:56.959
Speaker 3: Not not suggesting sabotage, I'm
suggesting that Georgians don't trust voting

00:02:56.959 --> 00:03:00.739
right now, and he took actions that led to
a lack of confidence.

00:03:00.739 --> 00:03:02.719
Speaker 1: Wow.

00:03:02.719 --> 00:03:09.680
Well, if Brad Raffensperger took actions that
led to a lack of confidence and he supported

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:15.550
Kelly Lefler, we should be looking into whether
Kelly Lefler really only lost by a little

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.420
bit to Raphael Warnock.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.870
Maybe Kelly Lefler lost by a lot.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:25.370
But Brad Raffensperger in the same way that
he may be pulled funny business against Trump

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.389
because he didn't like Trump.

00:03:27.389 --> 00:03:28.760
This is their story.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:33.199
Maybe he pulled some funny business in favor
of David Perdue and Kelly Lefler, who he supported.

00:03:33.199 --> 00:03:35.760
Now, of course, what's the truth here?

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:40.859
The truth is, I think Kelly Lefler knows the
Georgia election was pretty fair.

00:03:40.859 --> 00:03:42.659
Trump simply lost.

00:03:42.659 --> 00:03:46.719
She has sort of played coy with all of this
stuff because remember that there was that

00:03:46.719 --> 00:03:52.180
period between November and January where
Kelly Lefler and David Perdue were campaigning

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.489
for those special elections.

00:03:53.489 --> 00:03:57.670
She was fighting for her political life between
November and January 5th, which was the day

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.489
of that special election.

00:03:59.489 --> 00:04:02.799
And during that time, she needed Donald Trump's
support.

00:04:02.799 --> 00:04:04.469
At least she believed she needed it.

00:04:04.469 --> 00:04:07.019
I don't know, maybe it hurt more than helped.

00:04:07.019 --> 00:04:12.779
So she was playing coy with the election fraud
stuff when she was asked directly whether

00:04:12.779 --> 00:04:16.280
she agreed with Donald Trump that the election
in Georgia was rigged.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:20.769
I think during the debate with Raphael Warnock,
it came up, she would say stuff like, well,

00:04:20.769 --> 00:04:23.050
we need to investigate.

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:28.990
The president has every right to demand this
and that to his satisfaction that this was

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:30.860
done correctly and that was done correctly.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:36.220
We need to ensure every vote, every legal
vote is counted and every voice is heard.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:39.750
She was playing coy with it to avoid having
to say no.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:44.490
I think Trump's telling UBS, but then that
risks losing the Trump support she thought

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:47.470
she needed in that special election in January.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:50.060
I believe she doesn't care about Trump.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:51.699
I think she cares about herself.

00:04:51.699 --> 00:04:55.270
I think Kelly Lefler probably recognizes that
Trump's a disaster.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:59.840
But if Trump is useful to her, if it helps
her win, then she'll say whatever and accept

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:00.870
Donald Trump's support.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:02.919
She might want to run again.

00:05:02.919 --> 00:05:06.909
And she's probably looking at the same polls
we're looking at, which show that at least

00:05:06.909 --> 00:05:11.009
for right now, Donald Trump is a player in
Republican politics.

00:05:11.009 --> 00:05:14.210
She might need Trump's help if she wants to
run again.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:19.880
And she's going to keep playing coy and continuing
to be unable to just answer simple questions

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:24.990
are unable refusing to answer questions like
this one, which is, you know, the guy you're

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:29.330
saying we need to investigate supported you
in twenty twenty.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:33.380
So where does that leave us with any of this
nonsense?

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:39.229
I was hoping that the last we'd see of Carly
Lefler was when she lost to Raphael Warnock

00:05:39.229 --> 00:05:40.620
in January.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.419
Appears not to be the case.

00:05:42.419 --> 00:05:49.300
And she is truly detestable and so horrible
for the country and seems as determined as

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:53.340
ever to get involved again and to do more
damage.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:59.120
You almost get the sense that Kelly Lefler
is like surprised she's being asked this question

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.800
on Fox, which I mean, listen, it's sort of
surprising.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:07.600
But occasionally Neil Cavuto will ask what
we would call a real question that in other

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:11.050
countries, just every interview would have
real questions like this.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:15.849
And she's asked a so-called real question,
and she's unable to string together anything

00:06:15.849 --> 00:06:21.750
approximating a coherent response because
her position on this is and has been incoherent,

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.069
incoherent, like Trump.

00:06:24.069 --> 00:07:32.069
She may run again and we will need to fight
her if that's indeed what happens.

